///
/// Each day is closed from the date the vendored text was retrieved
/// (October 29, 2026; the PDFs carry no as-of date). Not modeled: Good
/// Friday, whose date § 311 leaves "As Designated in the Annual Calendar",
/// which is not vendored, so a last day on it stays the earlier date.
calendar northern-mariana-islands-holidays cite "1 CMC § 311"
{
  commonwealth-covenant-day: fixed(3, 24) effective [2026-10-29, ..) observed nearest_weekday
  citizenship-day: fixed(11, 4) effective [2026-10-29, ..) observed nearest_weekday
  constitution-day: fixed(12, 8) effective [2026-10-29, ..) observed nearest_weekday
}

/// The legal holidays of Nevada (NRS 236.015(1)) that `us-federal-holidays`
/// does not already close: Nevada Day, observed on the last Friday in
/// October, and Family Day, the Friday following the fourth Thursday in
/// November. NRS 236.015(2) closes the courts on them, and FRCP 6(a)(6)(C)
/// and FRBP 9006(a)(6)(C) make them legal holidays of the District of Nevada
/// for a period counted forward only (core's `frcp6-nevada` and
/// `frbp9006-nevada`). The other (1) days are federal holidays on the same
/// days, observed as (3) and § 6103(b)(1) both observe them.
///
/// Each day is closed from the date the vendored text is dated (the
/// chapter's revision of April 15, 2026) to the end of 2050. Not modeled:
/// October 31 itself, which (1) names as Nevada Day but does not observe;
/// and the days the President appoints, which no vendored source lists.
calendar nevada-holidays cite "NRS 236.015(1)"
{
  nevada-day: last(friday, 10) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  // The Friday following the fourth Thursday in November.
  family-day-2026: once(2026-11-27) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2027: once(2027-11-26) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2028: once(2028-11-24) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2029: once(2029-11-23) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2030: once(2030-11-29) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2031: once(2031-11-28) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2032: once(2032-11-26) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2033: once(2033-11-25) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2034: once(2034-11-24) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2035: once(2035-11-23) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2036: once(2036-11-28) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2037: once(2037-11-27) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2038: once(2038-11-26) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2039: once(2039-11-25) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2040: once(2040-11-23) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2041: once(2041-11-29) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2042: once(2042-11-28) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2043: once(2043-11-27) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2044: once(2044-11-25) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2045: once(2045-11-24) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2046: once(2046-11-23) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2047: once(2047-11-29) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2048: once(2048-11-27) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2049: once(2049-11-26) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
  family-day-2050: once(2050-11-25) effective [2026-04-15, ..)
}

/// The legal holidays of Oregon (ORS 187.010(1)) add no day
/// `us-federal-holidays` does not already close: each enumerated day is a
/// federal holiday on the same day, observed as § 6103(b)(1) observes it
/// (ORS 187.010(2)), and every Sunday is closed by `weekend`. The calendar
/// is declared, empty, so the District of Oregon's bankruptcy count (core's
/// `frbp9006-oregon`) names the state whose FRBP 9006(a)(6)(C) days it
/// reads. Not modeled: the days the Governor appoints (ORS 187.020), which
/// no vendored source lists.
calendar oregon-holidays cite "ORS 187.010(1)"
{}
